---
id: med-localpref
title: BGP MED and local preference
summary: Two exits to one client LAN; follow ICMP as MED and local preference change the selected path.
headline: Choose the exit, watch the ping

instructions: |
  Explore how BGP attributes change the ICMP path.

                    AS 65002
                  +-- edge1 --+
  client1 -- r1 --+           +-- shared LAN -- client2
         AS 65001 +-- edge2 --+

  Launch, wait for BGP, then use client1's ping action. Both edges advertise
  203.0.113.0/24 with equal AS paths; r1 initially prefers edge1's lower MED.
  Inspect r1's BGP routes and FIB, and follow ICMP echo requests in the animation.

  Experiments: edit the values below, then Reset/Launch to apply each change.
  1. Initial: edge1 MED 10, edge2 MED 50; both inbound bgp.locpref 100.
     Echo requests: client1 -> r1 -> edge1 -> client2.
  2. Change bgp.med on edge1’s interface toward r1 to 100. Lower MED now selects edge2.
     Echo requests: client1 -> r1 -> edge2 -> client2.
  3. Keep those MEDs; set bgp.locpref on r1’s interface toward edge1 to 200.
     Higher local preference overrides MED: requests use edge1 again.

  The edges set MED on their advertisements; r1 sets local preference on import.
  Local preference is internal to the receiving AS and is not sent over eBGP.
  MED is compared here because both paths come from the same neighboring AS.
  client2 always uses edge1 as its default gateway, so echo replies use edge1
  in every stage. Stage 2 deliberately demonstrates asymmetric traffic flow.
  edge1 also keeps a static route for 192.0.2.0/24 via edge2 at distance 250.
  eBGP (distance 20) wins while the r1 session is up. With r1–edge1 down, that
  static is installed and replies go client2 -> edge1 -> edge2 -> r1.

  Validation below describes stage 1 (also the winning next hop in stage 3).
  For stage 2 change the destination-route nexthop check to edge2.ipv4.r1.

topology:
  name: med-localpref
  device: frr
  module: [bgp]
  plugin: [bgp.policy]
  bgp:
    sessions:
      ipv4: [ebgp]
      ipv6: []

  nodes:
    lan:
      device: switch
      role: switch
    r1:
      bgp:
        as: 65001
        locpref: 100
    edge1:
      bgp:
        as: 65002
        advertise: [203.0.113.0/24]
      routing:
        static:
          - ipv4: client1.prefix
            nexthop: edge2.ipv4.lan
            distance: 250
    edge2:
      bgp:
        as: 65002
        advertise: [203.0.113.0/24]
    client1:
      device: linux
      role: host
      validation:
        actions:
          - label: Follow ICMP to client2
            type: ping
            target: client2
            count: 5
    client2:
      device: linux
      role: host
      routing:
        static:
          - ipv4: 0.0.0.0/0
            nexthop: 203.0.113.1
      validation:
        actions:
          - label: Ping back to client1
            type: ping
            target: client1
            count: 3

  links:
    - interfaces:
        - node: r1
          bgp:
            locpref: 100
        - node: edge1
          bgp:
            med: 10
    - interfaces:
        - node: r1
          bgp:
            locpref: 100
        - node: edge2
          bgp:
            med: 50
    - prefix:
        ipv4: 192.0.2.0/24
      interfaces:
        - node: r1
          ipv4: 192.0.2.1/24
        - node: client1
          ipv4: 192.0.2.10/24
    - prefix:
        ipv4: 203.0.113.0/24
      interfaces:
        - node: edge1
          ipv4: 203.0.113.1/24
        - node: lan
          ipv4: false
    - prefix:
        ipv4: 203.0.113.0/24
      interfaces:
        - node: edge2
          ipv4: 203.0.113.2/24
        - node: lan
          ipv4: false
    - prefix:
        ipv4: 203.0.113.0/24
      interfaces:
        - node: client2
          ipv4: 203.0.113.10/24
        - node: lan
          ipv4: false

  validate:
    - label: Both eBGP paths are available
      state:
        - node: r1
          bgp:
            - peer: edge1
              asn: edge1.asn
              state: established
            - peer: edge2
              asn: edge2.asn
              state: established
    - label: Lower MED selects edge1 with equal local preference
      state:
        - node: r1
          routes:
            - prefix: 203.0.113.0/24
              protocol: bgp
              nexthop: edge1.ipv4.r1
    - label: Both edges have a return route to client1
      state:
        - node: edge1
          routes:
            - prefix: 192.0.2.0/24
              protocol: bgp
              nexthop: r1.ipv4.edge1
        - node: edge2
          routes:
            - prefix: 192.0.2.0/24
              protocol: bgp
              nexthop: r1.ipv4.edge2
    - label: ICMP reaches client2 and returns
      packet:
        from: client1
        type: icmp-echo
        target: client2.ipv4
        expect:
          type: icmp-echo-reply
          from: client2
---
